        "subject": "LU-19672 idl: reserve OBD_CONNECT2_BATCH_DESTROY flag",
        "message": "LU-19672 idl: reserve OBD_CONNECT2_BATCH_DESTROY flag\n\nReserve OBD_CONNECT2_BATCH_DESTROY at 0x80000000000000ULL for a\ntarget that accepts OUT updates which tolerate -ENOENT, so the OSP\ncan batch object destroys.  Only the flag, obd_connect_names[] and\nthe wire checks are added here so the value can land before the\nfeature patch.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I5c0f67494f751c01572560cbdcc4733024402c27\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69535\nReviewed-by: Sebastien Buisson <sbuisson@ddn.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Alexander Boyko <alexander.boyko@hpe.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
